"comparison": "Both JPMorganChase and Goldman Sachs disclose that market volatility and illiquid conditions create significant challenges in valuing and trading financial instruments, with direct impacts on earnings. JPMorganChase highlights that market volatility and illiquid conditions may make it extremely difficult to value certain financial instruments (jpm_2024_1A_P070_S002). Goldman Sachs expands on this by noting that sudden declines and significant volatility can curtail trading markets, making it difficult to sell, hedge, or value assets (gs_2024_1A_P024_S003). Furthermore, both firms acknowledge the difficulty of hedging during these events; JPMorgan notes the inability to effectively hedge risks related to market-making positions (jpm_2024_1A_P052_S005), while Goldman Sachs states that declines in asset values directly impact earnings unless exposures are effectively hedged (gs_2024_1A_P023_S004).",
